From: Jay Heidecker <jay.heidecker@vcura.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: advertise HT40 only when rtw_bw_mode allows it

rtw_cfg80211_init_ht_capab() always set IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SUP_WIDTH_20_40,
even with rtw_bw_mode limiting the band to 20 MHz. The driver honors
rtw_bw_mode for its own links, but wpa_supplicant reads the cfg80211
capability to estimate throughput, so it kept ranking 40 MHz APs as twice
as fast and chose them over stronger 20 MHz APs with the same SSID.

Set SUP_WIDTH_20_40, SGI_40 and DSSSCCK40 only when rtw_bw_mode allows
40 MHz on the band.

--- a/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c
+++ b/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c
@@ -9169,9 +9169,18 @@
 
 	ht_cap->ht_supported = 1;
 
-	ht_cap->cap = IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SUP_WIDTH_20_40 |
-				IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SGI_40 | IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SGI_20 |
-				IEEE80211_HT_CAP_DSSSCCK40 | IEEE80211_HT_CAP_MAX_AMSDU;
+	ht_cap->cap = IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SGI_20 | IEEE80211_HT_CAP_MAX_AMSDU;
+
+	/*
+	 * Advertise 40 MHz only when rtw_bw_mode allows it on this band. The
+	 * driver already limits its own links to 20 MHz when it doesn't, but
+	 * cfg80211 kept reporting HT40, so wpa_supplicant still ranked 40 MHz
+	 * APs as twice as fast and preferred them over stronger 20 MHz ones.
+	 */
+	if ((band == BAND_ON_2_4G && REGSTY_IS_BW_2G_SUPPORT(regsty, CHANNEL_WIDTH_40))
+		|| (band == BAND_ON_5G && REGSTY_IS_BW_5G_SUPPORT(regsty, CHANNEL_WIDTH_40)))
+		ht_cap->cap |= IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SUP_WIDTH_20_40 |
+				IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SGI_40 | IEEE80211_HT_CAP_DSSSCCK40;
 	rtw_cfg80211_init_ht_capab_ex(padapter, ht_cap, band, rf_type);
 
 	/*
